## Playwright tests with every change

Every new or changed feature ships with matching Playwright coverage in `playwright/`; see the "Playwright tests with every change" section of `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md`.

- Add or update the specs under `playwright/tests/api` and `playwright/tests/ui` in the same change, and run the affected specs before declaring it complete.
- Do not delete, disable, or weaken existing tests to make a change pass.
- This is a student capstone: implement only required behavior and avoid unnecessary complexity.

# Language and path rules

- Reply to the user in **English only**. Do not use Chinese in chat, commits, comments, or project files.
- All new or edited project text must be English: Markdown, YAML/JSON comments, Java/JS comments, OpenAPI descriptions, commit messages.
- Do not leave leftover Chinese in files you touch. Translate it; do not delete meaning.

## Markdown paths

Never write a machine-specific absolute path in `*.md`:

- Bad: `D:\Documents\...`, `C:\Users\...`, `/Users/...`, `/home/...`
- Good: repo-relative paths such as `design/SCOPE-BASELINE.md`, `backend/java/dealer-core/src/main/resources/db/migration/V1__init.sql`

Use GitHub URLs or env-var placeholders (`$JAVA_HOME`, sibling checkout named `ai-manager`) instead of a local disk layout.

```md
<!-- BAD -->
Source: `D:\Documents\Capstone\DealerOps`

<!-- GOOD -->
Source: `design/IMPLEMENTATION-BRIEF.md` in this repository
```
